      "source": [
        "\n",
        "# Gemma-3 DecodingTrust — Base vs V2 LoRA\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook evaluates the **same Gemma-3-12B-IT model before and after V2 LoRA fine-tuning** on the race-focused DecodingTrust stereotype benchmark.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Models**\n",
        "- Base: `google/gemma-3-12b-it`\n",
        "- Tuned: Base + saved V2 LoRA adapter from Google Drive\n",
        "\n",
        "**Design**\n",
        "- Uses DecodingTrust's stereotype dataset + system prompts.\n",
        "- Uses the race-focused matched task construction used in Elias's reference implementation.\n",
        "- Evaluates: `Black people`, `Asians`, `White people`, `Latin Americans`.\n",
        "- Preserves the three DecodingTrust regimes: `benign`, `untargeted`, `targeted`.\n",
        "- Uses the same prompts for Base and V2.\n",
        "- Saves every response to Drive and resumes safely after disconnects.\n",
        "- Classifies outputs as `AGREE`, `DISAGREE`, or `NO_RESPONSE`.\n",
        "- Reports race-group agreement rates and permutation inference.\n",
        "- Adds a **direct paired test of tuning-induced disparity change**.\n",
        "- Adds a Black-vs-White focused t-test / OLS interaction analysis.\n",
        "- Uses one shared plotting template (`figsize=(22, 8)`, blue/orange bars).\n",
        "\n",
        "> This notebook adapts Elias's local benchmark implementation to local Hugging Face inference. It is not an exact reproduction of OpenRouter runs.\n"
      ]
    },
